sec.p:
At the end of the cultivation period (30 days), plant height, width, and circumference were measured using a ruler. Stem diameter and length were measured with a digital caliper (Mitutoyo, Tokyo, Japan). The number of leaves per plant was counted directly. Fresh weights of whole plants, leaves, and roots were measured using a digital precision balance with a sensitivity of 0.01 g. For dry weight determination, plant samples were oven-dried at 65 °C for 48 h until a constant weight was reached [79]. Dry matter content was calculated according to the following formula:\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
                                                  \usepackage{amsmath}
                                                  \usepackage{wasysym}
                                                  \usepackage{amsfonts}
                                                  \usepackage{amssymb}
                                                  \usepackage{amsbsy}
                                                  \usepackage{mathrsfs}
                                                  \usepackage{upgreek}
                                                  \setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
                                                  \begin{document}$$\text{Dry matter} (\%)=(\mathrm{Dry}\mathrm{weight} / \mathrm{Fresh}\mathrm{weight}) \times\;100$$\end{document}
